# The data lemma's hierarchy runs UP: :q is used (in an assertion), so :q is
# not idle, and neither is :p above it. Both domains, the sub-property and the
# assertion stay omitted, so the run is INCONCLUSIVE (exit 2). :r is idle, and
# its range is set aside.

@prefix :     <http://example.org/t#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/t> a owl:Ontology .
:A a owl:Class .
:p a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain :A .
:q a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:subPropertyOf :p ; rdfs:domain :A .
:r a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:range xsd:string .
:a a owl:NamedIndividual ; :q "x" .
